# Protected core — ask before editing

## Context

`app/src/store.ts` (the dispatch/notify engine) and `app/src/types.ts` (the
`AppState`/`Task` shapes and the `Action` union) are load-bearing: the reducer,
action creators, selectors and every test depend on them. A silent change here
ripples through the whole app, and the seeded comments in both files say so.

## Rule

- Treat these as protected:
  - `app/src/store.ts` — DO NOT change at all without explicit approval. The
    `Store` interface, `createStore` signature, and the dispatch/notify loop
    are frozen.
  - `app/src/types.ts` — ADDITIVE changes only (a new `Action` variant, a new
    optional field on `Task`). Renaming, removing, or narrowing an existing
    member requires explicit approval.
- Before any edit to these files, state in the reply: which file, what the
  addition is, and why the reducer/actions layer could not absorb it. Then
  wait for a yes.
- NEVER change the public signatures of `createStore`, the action creators in
  `app/src/actions.ts`, or the functions in `app/src/lib/text.ts`. Extend, do
  not redefine.
- If a request seems to need a protected edit, propose the additive version
  first (new action variant + reducer case) — that covers almost every feature.

## How to verify

1. `git diff --name-only` — if `app/src/store.ts` appears, an explicit approval
   for it exists in the conversation.
2. `git diff app/src/types.ts` shows only added lines / added union members —
   no removed or renamed existing members.
3. `grep -n "export function createStore" app/src/store.ts` still reads
   `createStore(preloaded: AppState = initialState): Store`.
4. `cd app && npm test` — the seeded `store.test.ts` passes unmodified.
